Geohash Native V2

Original extension: Geohash, by alrico88, MIT.
https://github.com/raycast/extensions/tree/6734d85992290066fd31a7f5bee3cca3d3545a1a/extensions/geohash-encode-decode
The pinned TS/TSX source, original package metadata and repository MIT license
are retained in tests/fixtures/upstream. provenance.json records original paths,
lengths and SHA-256 hashes. These fixtures are executed to generate the oracle.
The supplemental src/types/ngeohash.d.ts is from retained Tezbar V1, not upstream;
it is not loaded by the oracle evaluator.

Native Rust implementation and adapter: Copyright (c) 2026 almatkai, MIT.
See LICENSE. The root V1 package's existing files and license remain intact.

command-icon.png is the exact original Raycast Geohash icon (172526 bytes),
SHA-256 f59d02918ee4879a95940e3df317ff70ebeb901582967188b034b73daf0ee834.
It is copied without resizing, recompression, repainting or other modification.

Algorithm and serialization compatibility references:
- ngeohash 0.6.3, Copyright (c) 2011 Sun Ning, MIT; see licenses/ngeohash.txt.
- geohash-to-geojson 4.1.0, MIT; see licenses/geohash-to-geojson.txt.
- wkt-parser-helper 4.0.1, MIT; see licenses/wkt-parser-helper.txt.
- wellknown 0.5.0, WTFPL; see licenses/wellknown.txt.
- @sindresorhus/is 4.2.1, MIT; see licenses/sindresorhus-is.txt.
The Rust port implements only the operations exposed by the original two commands.
The JavaScript dependencies are optional oracle development tools, never executed
by the Native V2 runtime. Their exact resolved versions and integrity records are
in oracle/package-lock.json (copied unchanged from V1).

Tezbar beta API fixtures:
https://github.com/almatkai/Tezbar at fd300e276356587726566026f072563eb9c34cb1.
tests/fixtures/beta/{common.rs,v2_sdk.rs,extension-v2.schema.json,LICENSE}
are byte-exact copies of the paths in that directory's provenance.json, under
the Apache License 2.0. See tests/fixtures/beta/LICENSE. No fixture modifications.
The test harness supplies a minimal Tauri surface stub; this is separate from
those files. The real CoreContext and SDK code, including their tests, compile
and execute without desktop OS effects.

The distributable crate includes both MIT extension code and Apache-2.0 beta
fixtures, so its package SPDX expression is MIT AND Apache-2.0. Individual
third-party Cargo dependencies retain their own licenses (see Cargo.lock and
Cargo metadata); ryu-js is Apache-2.0 OR BSL-1.0. Bundling dependencies or the
optional npm oracle tooling requires retaining their respective license notices.
